---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/case-base.css";

const title = "FLAX Hospitality — Product Marketing & Brand | Maria Klammer";
---

<Base title={title} noWrap={false} hideFooter={false}>
  <article class="container-narrow doc-grid tokens-case">
    <nav class="case-rail case-rail--left" aria-label="Previous project">
      <a class="pager-btn pager-btn--prev" href="/case-studies/email-marketing" aria-label="Previous: Email Marketing Platform">
        <svg class="pager-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 12H5"/><path d="M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </nav>
    <div class="doc-main">
      <header class="case-hero">
        <h1>FLAX Hospitality POS<br>product marketing,<br>web & social direction</h1>
        <p class="meta">Product design • UX/UI • Brand direction • Frontend • Social content • 2026</p>
        <p class="lede">
          Built a clearer international-facing product story for FLAX, a configurable hospitality POS platform.
          The work connects the English product site and social presence into one visual and messaging system,
          with a stronger focus on real restaurant workflows, offline support and flexible configuration.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="hero-vertical" aria-label="FLAX website preview">
        <button class="shot-tile ar-21x9"
          data-full="/images/flax/hero.webp"
          data-title="Hospitality-led hero"
          data-cap="<p>A darker editorial direction positions FLAX around real service environments rather than generic software imagery.</p>">
          <img src="/images/flax/hero.webp" alt="FLAX Hospitality website hero" />
        </button>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Positioning</h2>
        <p>
          The site needed to feel like a hospitality product first, not a generic POS feature catalogue. I reframed
          the product around the restaurant workflow: POS, tables, orders, kitchen, payments, delivery integrations,
          loyalty and multi-location management — while keeping the core messages around configurability and offline support visible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What I worked on</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Web UX/UI:</strong> structured the English landing page around restaurant workflows, product capability and service context.</li>
          <li><strong>Visual direction:</strong> created a darker, editorial hospitality look combining real-world imagery with product UI.</li>
          <li><strong>Product storytelling:</strong> translated a broad POS feature set into clear sections for restaurants, cafés, bars and hotels.</li>
          <li><strong>Brand consistency:</strong> carried the same tone, typography and visual language into FLAX social content.</li>
          <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> implemented and iterated the landing page, responsive sections and product presentation.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>From product UI to brand content</h2>
        <p>
          The website alternates between service photography and actual interface views so the product stays credible
          while still feeling aspirational. For Instagram, the same system becomes shorter campaign stories around QR,
          integrations, offline operation, product UI and restaurant scenarios.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Result</h2>
        <p>
          FLAX now has a more coherent international presentation across web and social: a recognisable visual voice,
          clearer hospitality positioning and a product story that can support campaigns in multiple markets without
          losing the underlying technical strengths.
        </p>
        <p class="case-links">
          <a class="btn link-btn" href="https://resto.flax.com/en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="btn-label">View FLAX website</span></a>
          <a class="btn link-btn" href="https://www.instagram.com/flaxpos.global/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="btn-label">View Instagram</span></a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="doc-aside feature-card">
      <nav class="shots-grid" aria-label="FLAX project gallery">
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/workspace.webp" data-title="Product workspace" data-cap="<p>Core platform benefits paired with the POS interface.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/workspace.webp" alt="FLAX product workspace section" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/verticals.webp" data-title="Hospitality verticals" data-cap="<p>Restaurant, café, bar and hotel scenarios make the target audience explicit.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/verticals.webp" alt="FLAX restaurant cafe bar hotel section" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/product-ui.webp" data-title="Product UI" data-cap="<p>Large product UI presentation keeps the interface itself central to the story.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/product-ui.webp" alt="FLAX POS interface" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/features.webp" data-title="Feature architecture" data-cap="<p>Feature groups are presented as an operating system for the restaurant rather than a flat checklist.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/features.webp" alt="FLAX feature grid" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/brand.webp" data-title="Brand story" data-cap="<p>The about section establishes experience, Estonian roots, international reach and local support.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/brand.webp" alt="FLAX brand story section" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/ecosystem.webp" data-title="Product ecosystem" data-cap="<p>Cross-links connect FLAX to related self-service, mobile POS and WMS solutions.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/ecosystem.webp" alt="FLAX related solutions section" /></button>
        <button class="shot-tile" data-full="/images/flax/instagram.webp" data-title="Global Instagram direction" data-cap="<p>Social content extends the same product-and-hospitality visual language into campaign-sized stories.</p>"><img src="/images/flax/instagram.webp" alt="FLAX Instagram grid" /></button>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <div class="tokens-lightbox" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="tokens-lightbox__dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Image preview">
        <button class="tokens-lightbox__close" type="button" aria-label="Close">×</button>
        <button class="tokens-lightbox__nav tokens-lightbox__prev" aria-label="Previous image">‹</button>
        <button class="tokens-lightbox__nav tokens-lightbox__next" aria-label="Next image">›</button>
        <div class="tokens-lightbox__media"><img class="tokens-lightbox__img" alt="" /></div>
        <aside class="tokens-lightbox__meta"><h4 class="tokens-lightbox__title"></h4><div class="tokens-lightbox__cap"></div></aside>
      </div>
    </div>
      <nav class="case-rail case-rail--right" aria-label="Next project">
      <a class="pager-btn pager-btn--next" href="/case-studies/isekas" aria-label="Next: Isekas — Self-Service Checkout">
        <svg class="pager-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </nav>
</article>

  <script>
    import initLightbox from "../../scripts/case-lightbox";
    initLightbox();
  </script>
</Base>
